  "review": {
    "verdict": "PASS",
    "feedback": "The fixed module proves only the stated conditional divisibility results, not that the original equation is solved. cofactor_two_cube_dvd correctly shows q1=(i-1)/gcd(i-1,6) divides r^3 using q1 | choose(i,3)=A and q1 | X, with i=3,4 handled by q1=1. Q_cube_dvd correctly combines this with q0=i/gcd(i,3) | r^3; q0 and q1 are coprime because they divide consecutive integers i and i-1. The assumptions i≥3 and k≤A make A-k and all gcd/divisions legitimate, and min k (A-k) is the intended r. The names do not overstate the final result or claim Q is the full gcd. No nonzero/positive or scope issue found."
